%% Server-priced storefront checkout and order boundary
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Customer
    participant Web as Customer Web
    participant API as Checkout/Order API
    participant Cart as Cart service
    participant Checkout as Checkout service
    participant DB as Tenant PostgreSQL
    participant Payment as Payment gateway adapter
    participant Queue as Transactional queue
    participant Worker as Tenant-stamped worker
    participant Courier as Courier adapter

    Customer->>Web: Browse published catalog
    Web->>API: Read catalog using resolved tenant host
    API->>DB: Read published products and variants
    DB-->>API: Catalog projection
    API-->>Web: Catalog projection

    Customer->>Web: Add item and open checkout
    Web->>API: Cart token and requested item changes
    API->>Cart: Validate publication, price, and stock
    Cart->>DB: Read and update tenant cart
    DB-->>Cart: Current cart state

    Web->>API: POST checkout/preview
    API->>Checkout: Re-read mutable commerce facts
    Checkout->>DB: Price, stock, delivery, discount, and policy checks
    DB-->>Checkout: Server-priced checkout draft
    Checkout-->>Web: Totals and payment options

    alt Cash on delivery
        Web->>API: POST checkout/orders with idempotency key
        API->>DB: Transactionally create COD order and reserve inventory
        DB-->>API: Order reference
    else Prepaid
        Web->>API: Create prepaid order/payment attempt
        API->>DB: Create attempt and order state
        API->>Payment: Create hosted payment session
        Payment-->>Web: Provider redirect/session
        Payment->>API: Signed tenant-bound callback
        API->>Payment: Verify signature, amount, currency, replay state
        API->>DB: Transactionally finalize payment state
    end

    API->>Queue: Record deduplicated notification/fulfillment work
    Queue-->>API: Accepted for asynchronous processing
    Queue->>Worker: Deliver tenant-stamped job
    Worker->>Courier: Poll or send shipment workflow
    Courier-->>Worker: Normalized shipment event
    Worker->>DB: Persist shipment and order history
    API-->>Web: Stable order/payment status

    Note over API,DB: Idempotency prevents browser retries from duplicating orders.
    Note over Queue,Courier: Provider calls stay outside the order transaction.
